From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] LinkerOptimizationHints: complete the scrubbed valid()

The published mach_o/LinkerOptimizationHints.cpp has the body of
LinkerOptimizationHints::valid() removed down to its return statement, which
names a variable that no longer exists, so libmach_o doesn't compile. The
check only matters to the linker and verification tools; neither dyld nor
libdyld calls it. Return no error, as a binary without hints would.

Rebase-risk: low (one function; drop the patch when the body is published).
---
--- a/mach_o/LinkerOptimizationHints.cpp
+++ b/mach_o/LinkerOptimizationHints.cpp
@@ -121,8 +121,9 @@
 
 Error LinkerOptimizationHints::valid(std::span<const MappedSegment> segments, uint64_t loadAddress) const
 {
-
-    return std::move(lohErr);
+    // NeoDarwin: the published source has this function's body removed; no
+    // check is made.
+    return Error::none();
 }
 
 } // namespace mach_o
